# 1. Driver operating model

## 1.1 Driver types

| Driver type | Best use |
|---|---|
| **Local scooter driver** | Short same-village or same-ridge deliveries, small hot-food orders |
| **150cc scooter driver** | Longer paved routes with moderate elevation |
| **Sedan driver** | Multi-order routes, weather, fragile orders, moderate cross-village travel |
| **4WD driver** | Steep terrain, poor roads, snow/rain, valley crossings, large orders |
| **Relief driver** | Peak periods, driver absence, overflow, failed delivery recovery |
| **Dispatch supervisor** | Assignment approval, exception handling, cash reconciliation, quality control |

Do not assign purely from vehicle type. Also record:

```text
vehicle_type
vehicle_condition
maximum_load
maximum_active_orders
approved_zones
terrain_capability
cash_limit
shift_hours
training_status
insurance_status
```

## 1.2 Driver modes

```text
offline
available
offered
assigned
at_pickup
picked_up
en_route
at_dropoff
awaiting_customer
completed
exception
returning
suspended
```

A driver who is `at_dropoff` or `awaiting_customer` must not receive another order unless the dispatch engine explicitly authorizes it.

## 1.3 Driver availability

Drivers should be able to use:

```text
Go online
Go offline
Pause for fuel
Pause for prayer/break
Vehicle issue
Emergency
End shift
```

A driver cannot go offline while carrying active orders unless dispatch accepts the handoff or return plan.

