# 9. Batching control in detail

## 9.1 Batch eligibility record

Every batch decision should be explainable:

```json
{
  "batch_id": "batch_123",
  "driver_id": "driver_456",
  "orders": ["order_a", "order_b"],
  "reason_codes": [
    "same_restaurant",
    "same_delivery_corridor",
    "ready_times_compatible",
    "eta_buffer_maintained",
    "vehicle_capacity_ok"
  ],
  "predicted_late_risk": 0.08,
  "predicted_extra_minutes": 6,
  "approved_by": "dispatch_engine",
  "created_at": "..."
}
```

## 9.2 Batch rejection reasons

```text
opposite_directions
late_risk_too_high
food_quality_risk
terrain_mismatch
weather_risk
cash_limit
driver_capacity
restaurant_not_ready
customer_priority_order
```

## 9.3 Customer transparency

Do not tell the customer that another customer’s order is in the car. Simply provide the correct ETA.

If batching causes a delay, Alo King should not hide it. Notify the customer with a revised estimate and offer support when the delay crosses the policy threshold.

