# 13. Recommended first launch policy

For the first operational pilot:

```text
Default: one order per driver
Batching: maximum two orders
Allowed batching: same restaurant or same corridor only
No cross-valley batching
No batching in severe weather
No batching for fragile/temperature-sensitive orders
Every batch requires engine approval
Every batch must preserve promised ETA buffer
Every driver gets a clear cash limit
Every delivery requires proof event
Every exception has a reason code
```

Run this for at least several weeks while measuring:

- actual route time;
- pickup wait;
- on-time delivery;
- food quality complaints;
- batch delay versus single-order baseline;
- driver earnings;
- driver acceptance/decline reasons;
- customer satisfaction;
- cash discrepancy;
- failed delivery rate.

Only expand batching when data proves that customers and drivers benefit.

