# 15. Final answer to the main question

## Should one driver carry one order or pick up a second order?

Use this rule:

> **One order is the default. A second order is allowed only when the dispatch engine confirms same-direction routing, compatible preparation times, safe vehicle capacity, protected ETA, acceptable food quality, and cash limits.**

For Alo King’s initial Shouf operation:

- one order for most routes;
- two orders for same-restaurant or same-corridor routes;
- never allow arbitrary driver self-batching;
- never let batching compromise the first customer’s promised delivery;
- use cars/4WDs for cross-valley and difficult terrain;
- use scooters for short local routes;
- begin with a conservative two-drop maximum.

> The objective is not to maximize drops per driver. It is to maximize **profitable, safe, on-time completed deliveries**.
